{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"oozy-cabbagy-tuna","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Rename --force-close to --force for consistency with other flags\n\n## Context\nOperator decision 2026-08-04 (bug-triage session): the close gate on LLM provider error is being made fail-closed (bug 1019), with the force flag as the escape hatch. claim already spells its escape hatch --force[=<reason>]; transition spells it --force-close. One concept, two spellings.\n\n## Plan\n- Rename the transition flag to --force[=<reason>], matching claim.\n- Keep --force-close as a deprecated alias for one release window (warn on use), so in-flight agent instructions and docs do not break atomically.\n- Update usage text, AGENTS.md/docs references, and verify force flags stay CLI-only (not exposed over MCP).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] rebar transition <id> <from> closed --force[=reason] bypasses the close gate exactly as --force-close did.\n- [ ] --force-close still works but emits a deprecation warning naming --force.\n- [ ] All in-repo docs/guides reference --force; grep finds no bare --force-close outside the deprecation shim.\n- [ ] Behavioral tests: force bypasses gate, deprecated alias warns and bypasses, no force flag over MCP.","id":"24f7-1955-bcd8-4f29","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Rename --force-close to --force on transition for flag consistency"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785860061323412001,"uuid":"0cdb64c2-cb7f-43b2-9bf0-9222dde2ffdc"}